#: simulation/templates/gaia/ruins/column_doric.xml:8
msgid "Doric Column"
msgstr "Dorisk kolumn"

#: simulation/templates/gaia/ruins/column_doric.xml:9
msgid ""
"\n"
"        A ruined Doric column that fell off of some building. There is little else to do but reuse the materials.\n"
"    "
msgstr ""
"\n"
"        En förstörd dorisk kolonn som har fallit från någon byggnad. Det finns inte mycket annat att göra än att återanvända materialet.\n"
"    "

#: simulation/templates/gaia/ruins/metal_statue_apollo.xml:9
msgid "Apollo"
msgstr "Apollo"

#: simulation/templates/gaia/ruins/metal_statue_apollo.xml:11
msgid ""
"\n"
"        A metal statue of the greek god Apollo. It is a nice statue, but could be also turned into metal for one of your own projects.\n"
"    "
msgstr ""
"\n"
"        En metallstaty av den grekiske guden Apollo. Den är fin, men metallen kan också användas i något av dina egna projekt.\n"
"    "

#: simulation/templates/gaia/ruins/metal_statue_caryatid.xml:9
msgid "Caryatid Statue"
msgstr "Karyatid-staty"

#: simulation/templates/gaia/ruins/metal_statue_caryatid.xml:11
msgid ""
"\n"
"        This is a Caryatid, a carved statue that is used as a column to support a building. it is now freestanding and its metal could be used for something nice, maybe some swords?\n"
"    "
msgstr ""
"\n"
"        Detta är en karyatid, en snidad staty som används som kolonn för att bära upp en byggnad. Den står nu fritt och metallen kan användas till något fint, kanske svärd?\n"
"    "

#: simulation/templates/gaia/ruins/metal_statue_discobolus.xml:8
msgid "Discobolus"
msgstr "Discobolus"

#: simulation/templates/gaia/ruins/metal_statue_discobolus.xml:10
msgid ""
"\n"
"        This is a metal reproduction of the Discobolus, a famous statue made by the Greek artist Myron. It depicts a Greek athlete throwing a discus.\n"
"    "
msgstr ""
"\n"
"        Detta är en metallreproduktion av Diskuskastaren, en berömd staty av den grekiske konstnären Myron. Den föreställer en grekisk idrottare som kastar diskus.\n"
"    "

#: simulation/templates/gaia/ruins/metal_statue_isis.xml:9
msgid "Isis Cult Image"
msgstr "Isis kultavbild"

#: simulation/templates/gaia/ruins/metal_statue_isis.xml:11
msgid ""
"\n"
"        A great metal statue of Isis, the Egyptian mother goddess. It’s nice if you like that sort of thing, but the material probably could be put to better use.\n"
"    "
msgstr ""
"\n"
"        En stor metallstaty av Isis, den egyptiska modergudinnan. Den är fin om man gillar den sortens saker, men materialet kan säkert användas bättre.\n"
"    "

#: simulation/templates/gaia/ruins/metal_statue_poseidon.xml:8
msgid "Poseidon"
msgstr "Poseidon"

#: simulation/templates/gaia/ruins/metal_statue_poseidon.xml:10
msgid ""
"\n"
"        A metal statue of Poseidon, the greek god of the sea. It is a nice statue, but could be also turned into some metal for one of your own projects.\n"
"    "
msgstr ""
"\n"
"        En metallstaty av Poseidon, den grekiske havsguden. Den är fin, men kan också smältas ned till metall för något av dina egna projekt.\n"
"    "

#: simulation/templates/gaia/ruins/metal_statue_wolf.xml:9
msgid "Capitoline Wolf"
msgstr "Kapitoliska vargen"

#: simulation/templates/gaia/ruins/metal_statue_wolf.xml:11
msgid ""
"\n"
"        A metal statue depicting a wolf who, according to legend, nursed Romulus and Remus, the brothers who built Rome.\n"
"    "
msgstr ""
"\n"
"        En metallstaty som föreställer en varghona som enligt legenden diade Romulus och Remus, bröderna som byggde Rom.\n"
"    "

#: simulation/templates/gaia/ruins/pyramid_great.xml:8
msgid "Great Pyramid"
msgstr "Stor pyramid"

#: simulation/templates/gaia/ruins/pyramid_great.xml:10
msgid ""
"\n"
"        This construction is a masterpiece of technology and architecture. Only countless years of intense labor and vast amounts of wealth could be spent to produce such a building. If left untouched, this pyramid will become a symbol; a monument to an ancient civilization, displaying their greatest achievements. But it is an awful lot of stone to just lie there undisturbed. Surely, you’d be able to use it to build something better?\n"
"    "
msgstr ""
"\n"
"        Denna konstruktion är ett mästerverk av teknik och arkitektur. Endast oräkneliga år av hårt arbete och enorma rikedomar kan ha skapat en sådan byggnad. Orörd blir pyramiden ett monument över en forntida civilisations främsta bedrifter. Men det är väldigt mycket sten som bara ligger där. Du kan säkert använda den till att bygga något bättre?\n"
"    "

#: simulation/templates/gaia/ruins/pyramid_minor.xml:8
msgid "Minor Pyramid"
msgstr "Mindre pyramid"

#: simulation/templates/gaia/ruins/pyramid_minor.xml:10
msgid ""
"\n"
"        Here stands a monument and tomb for some great person. It also is precisely where you wanted to build and so will have to be moved.\n"
"    "
msgstr ""
"\n"
"        Här står ett monument och en grav för någon stor person. Den står dessutom precis där du ville bygga och måste därför flyttas.\n"
"    "

#: simulation/templates/gaia/ruins/roman_rostrum.xml:8
msgid "Roman Rostrum"
msgstr "Romersk talarstol"

#: simulation/templates/gaia/ruins/roman_rostrum.xml:9
msgid ""
"\n"
"        A rostrum such as this one would be used in the period of the Roman Republic for senators to give speeches.\n"
"    "
msgstr ""
"\n"
"        En talarstol som denna användes under den romerska republiken av senatorer för att hålla tal.\n"
"    "

#: simulation/templates/gaia/ruins/standing_stone.xml:8
#: simulation/templates/gaia/treasure/standing_stone.xml:8
msgid "Celtic Standing Stone"
msgstr "Keltisk stående sten"

#: simulation/templates/gaia/ruins/standing_stone.xml:9
msgid ""
"\n"
"        A Celtic stone inscribed with mysterious markings. What could it be, a property marker? A monument? A secret message? Or is it just a lump of stone that you can use?\n"
"    "
msgstr ""
"\n"
"        En keltisk sten med mystiska inskrifter. Vad kan den vara: en ägomarkering, ett monument, ett hemligt meddelande? Eller bara en stenklump som du kan använda?\n"
"    "

#: simulation/templates/gaia/ruins/stone_column_roman.xml:8
msgid "Roman Column"
msgstr "Romersk kolonn"

#: simulation/templates/gaia/ruins/stone_column_roman.xml:9
msgid ""
"\n"
"        A stone column as those found in Roman buildings.\n"
"    "
msgstr ""
"\n"
"        En stenkolonn av den typ som finns i romerska byggnader.\n"
"    "

#: simulation/templates/gaia/ruins/stone_statues_achaemenid_lamassu.xml:8
msgid "Lamassu Statue"
msgstr "Lamassu-staty"

#: simulation/templates/gaia/ruins/stone_statues_achaemenid_lamassu.xml:9
msgid ""
"\n"
"        A stone statue of the Mesopotamian deity, Lamassu. While it looks nice, you could probably use the stone for something better.\n"
"    "
msgstr ""
"\n"
"        En stenstaty av den mesopotamiska gudomen Lamassu. Den ser fin ut, men stenen kan säkert användas till något bättre.\n"
"    "

#: simulation/templates/gaia/ruins/stone_statues_egyptian.xml:8
msgid "Egyptian Statue"
msgstr "Egyptisk staty"

#: simulation/templates/gaia/ruins/stone_statues_egyptian.xml:10
msgid ""
"\n"
"        Various stone statues of Egyptian royalty and religion. Its materials could easily be reused in other constructions.\n"
"    "
msgstr ""
"\n"
"        Olika stenstatyer av egyptiska kungligheter och religiösa gestalter. Materialet kan lätt återanvändas i andra konstruktioner.\n"
"    "

#: simulation/templates/gaia/ruins/stone_statues_kushite.xml:8
msgid "Kushite Statue"
msgstr "Kushitisk staty"

#: simulation/templates/gaia/ruins/stone_statues_kushite.xml:10
msgid ""
"\n"
"        Various stone statues of Kushite royalty and religion. Its materials could easily be reused in other constructions.\n"
"    "
msgstr ""
"\n"
"        Olika stenstatyer av kushitiska kungligheter och religiösa gestalter. Materialet kan lätt återanvändas i andra konstruktioner.\n"
"    "

#: simulation/templates/gaia/ruins/stone_statues_kushite_bird.xml:9
#: simulation/templates/gaia/ruins/stone_statues_kushite_lion.xml:9
#: simulation/templates/gaia/ruins/stone_statues_kushite_ram.xml:9
#: simulation/templates/gaia/ruins/stone_structure_farmstead.xml:9
#: simulation/templates/gaia/ruins/stone_structure_house.xml:9
#: simulation/templates/gaia/ruins/stone_structure_small.xml:9
#: simulation/templates/gaia/ruins/stone_structure_tower.xml:9
msgid "Stone Resource"
msgstr "Stenresurs"

#: simulation/templates/gaia/ruins/stone_statues_kushite_bird.xml:10
msgid "Kushite Bird Statue"
msgstr "Kushitefågelstaty"

#: simulation/templates/gaia/ruins/stone_statues_kushite_bird.xml:12
msgid ""
"\n"
"        This is an ancient Kushite statue of a bird. Its materials could easily be reused in other constructions.\n"
"    "
msgstr ""
"\n"
"        Detta är en forntida kushitisk staty av en fågel. Materialet kan lätt återanvändas i andra konstruktioner.\n"
"    "

#: simulation/templates/gaia/ruins/stone_statues_kushite_lion.xml:10
msgid "Apademak Lion Statue"
msgstr "Apademakisk lejonstaty"

#: simulation/templates/gaia/ruins/stone_statues_kushite_lion.xml:12
msgid ""
"\n"
"        In ancient Kush, lion statues were found in palaces and temples. They are the ultimate symbol of royal authority and also were associated with the god Apedemak. Its materials could easily be reused in other constructions.\n"
"    "
msgstr ""
"\n"
"        I det forntida Kush fanns lejonstatyer i palats och tempel. De var den främsta symbolen för kunglig auktoritet och förknippades även med guden Apedemak. Materialet kan lätt återanvändas i andra konstruktioner.\n"
"    "

#: simulation/templates/gaia/ruins/stone_statues_kushite_ram.xml:10
msgid "Ammon-Ra Ram Statue"
msgstr "Ammon-Ras baggestaty"

#: simulation/templates/gaia/ruins/stone_statues_kushite_ram.xml:12
msgid ""
"\n"
"        In ancient Kush, rams were the icon of their supreme god, Amun. The statue's materials could easily be reused in other constructions.\n"
"    "
msgstr ""
"\n"
"        I det forntida Kush var baggar symbolen för deras högste gud Amun. Statyns material kan lätt återanvändas i andra konstruktioner.\n"
"    "

#: simulation/templates/gaia/ruins/stone_statues_roman.xml:8
msgid "Roman Statue"
msgstr "Romersk staty"

#: simulation/templates/gaia/ruins/stone_statues_roman.xml:9
msgid ""
"\n"
"        Various stone statues of Roman royalty and religion. Its materials could easily be reused in other constructions.\n"
"    "
msgstr ""
"\n"
"        Olika stenstatyer av romerska kungligheter och religiösa gestalter. Materialet kan lätt återanvändas i andra konstruktioner.\n"
"    "

#: simulation/templates/gaia/ruins/stone_structure_farmstead.xml:10
msgid "Ruined Farmstead"
msgstr "Förstörd bondgård"

#: simulation/templates/gaia/ruins/stone_structure_farmstead.xml:12
#: simulation/templates/gaia/ruins/stone_structure_house.xml:11
msgid ""
"\n"
"       A house once stood here. Now, however, there are only the remains of its foundation. What had destroyed it? Invaders perhaps? Or maybe just the force of nature gradually taking its toll? Whatever the cause of its destruction, the remaining stone can be reclaimed.\n"
"    "
msgstr ""
"\n"
"       Här stod en gång ett hus. Nu återstår bara grunden. Vad förstörde det? Kanske angripare, eller naturens krafter? Oavsett orsaken kan den återstående stenen tas till vara.\n"
"    "

#: simulation/templates/gaia/ruins/stone_structure_house.xml:10
msgid "Ruined House"
msgstr "Förstört hus"

#: simulation/templates/gaia/ruins/stone_structure_small.xml:10
msgid "Ruined Structure"
msgstr "Förstörd byggnad"

#: simulation/templates/gaia/ruins/stone_structure_small.xml:11
msgid ""
"\n"
"        These ruins have been so destroyed that it is impossible to find what they once were. What the stone will be is a more pressing question.\n"
"    "
msgstr ""
"\n"
"        Dessa ruiner är så förstörda att det är omöjligt att avgöra vad de en gång var. Den viktigare frågan är vad stenen kan bli.\n"
"    "

#: simulation/templates/gaia/ruins/stone_structure_tower.xml:10
msgid "Ruined Tower"
msgstr "Förstört torn"

#: simulation/templates/gaia/ruins/stone_structure_tower.xml:12
msgid ""
"\n"
"        The start of a tower. Unfortunately, whoever started was not able to finish the work, so you’ll have to put what remains to good use.\n"
"    "
msgstr ""
"\n"
"        Början till ett torn. Tyvärr kunde den som påbörjade arbetet inte slutföra det, så du får använda resterna väl.\n"
"    "

#: simulation/templates/gaia/ruins/unfinished_greek_temple.xml:8
msgid "Unfinished Greek Temple"
msgstr "Ofärdigt grekiskt tempel"

#: simulation/templates/gaia/ruins/unfinished_greek_temple.xml:9
msgid ""
"\n"
"        The Greeks were excellent masons, and when completed, their structures will last for ages. Unfortunately, this temple was abandoned before it was finished, and now it is little more than a pile of stone waiting to be repurposed.\n"
"    "
msgstr ""
"\n"
"        Grekerna var skickliga murare och deras färdiga byggnader kan bestå i evigheter. Tyvärr övergavs detta tempel innan det blev klart och är nu mest en hög sten som väntar på att återanvändas.\n"
"    "

#: simulation/templates/gaia/treasure/food_achaemenid_big.xml:8
msgid "Persian Food Stores"
msgstr "Persiska matlager"

#: simulation/templates/gaia/treasure/food_achaemenid_big.xml:9
msgid ""
"\n"
"        A large display of food, straight from the finest bazars.\n"
"    "
msgstr ""
"\n"
"        En stor uppvisning av mat, direkt från de bästa basarerna.\n"
"    "

#: simulation/templates/gaia/treasure/food_achaemenid_small.xml:8
msgid "Persian Food Treasure"
msgstr "Persisk matskatt"

#: simulation/templates/gaia/treasure/food_achaemenid_small.xml:9
msgid ""
"\n"
"        A display of food, straight from the finest bazars.\n"
"    "
msgstr ""
"\n"
"        En uppvisning av mat, direkt från de bästa basarerna.\n"
"    "

#: simulation/templates/gaia/treasure/food_barrel.xml:8
#: simulation/templates/gaia/treasure/food_bin.xml:8
#: simulation/templates/gaia/treasure/food_crate.xml:8
#: simulation/templates/gaia/treasure/food_jars.xml:8
msgid "Food Treasure"
msgstr "Matskatt"

#: simulation/templates/gaia/treasure/food_barrel.xml:10
msgid ""
"\n"
"        This is a barrel of food. Wooden barrels were and still are an excellent way for storing both wet and dry foodstuffs.\n"
"    "
msgstr ""
"\n"
"        Detta är en tunna med mat. Trätunnor var och är ett utmärkt sätt att lagra både våta och torra livsmedel.\n"
"    "

#: simulation/templates/gaia/treasure/food_barrels_buried.xml:8
msgid "Half-buried Barrels"
msgstr "Halvnedgrävda tunnor"

#: simulation/templates/gaia/treasure/food_barrels_buried.xml:10
msgid ""
"\n"
"        A long forgotten cache of food. They were buried for safekeeping. However, over time, the soil has eroded, exposing them. Seeing that the original owners are long gone, it is probably best that you put the resources to good use before your opponents do.\n"
"    "
msgstr ""
"\n"
"        Ett sedan länge bortglömt matförråd. Det begravdes för säker förvaring, men med tiden har jorden eroderat och blottat det. Eftersom de ursprungliga ägarna är borta är det bäst att använda resurserna innan dina motståndare gör det.\n"
"    "

#: simulation/templates/gaia/treasure/food_bin.xml:10
msgid ""
"\n"
"        A bin of food.\n"
"    "
msgstr ""
"\n"
"        En låda med mat.\n"
"    "

#: simulation/templates/gaia/treasure/food_crate.xml:10
msgid ""
"\n"
"        A crate of food, packed as if it was going to be taken on a boat for a long journey.\n"
"    "
msgstr ""
"\n"
"        En låda med mat, packad som om den skulle tas med på båt under en lång resa.\n"
"    "

#: simulation/templates/gaia/treasure/food_jars.xml:10
msgid ""
"\n"
"        Food safely stored inside clay jars.\n"
"    "
msgstr ""
"\n"
"        Mat som förvaras säkert i lerkrukor.\n"
"    "

#: simulation/templates/gaia/treasure/golden_fleece.xml:8
msgid "Golden Fleece"
msgstr "Gyllene päls"

#: simulation/templates/gaia/treasure/golden_fleece.xml:9
msgid ""
"\n"
"        There are legends about sheep with golden wool. One was sent by Zeus to fly Phrixus to safety when his father was going to kill him. Another was found in the flock of Atreus. Both were extremely valuable, and undoubtedly this one is too.\n"
"    "
msgstr ""
"\n"
"        Det finns legender om får med gyllene ull. Ett sändes av Zeus för att föra Phrixos i säkerhet när hans far ville döda honom. Ett annat fanns i Atreus hjord. Båda var mycket värdefulla och detta är utan tvekan det också.\n"
"    "

#: simulation/templates/gaia/treasure/metal.xml:8
msgid "Secret Box"
msgstr "Hemlig låda"

#: simulation/templates/gaia/treasure/metal.xml:9
msgid ""
"\n"
"        It's a barrel filled with metal.\n"
"        There. I ruined the secret.\n"
"    "
msgstr ""
"\n"
"        Det är en tunna fylld med metall.\n"
"        Så. Nu avslöjade jag hemligheten.\n"
"    "

#: simulation/templates/gaia/treasure/metal_achaemenid_big.xml:8
msgid "Persian Wares"
msgstr "Persiska varor"

#: simulation/templates/gaia/treasure/metal_achaemenid_big.xml:9
#: simulation/templates/gaia/treasure/metal_achaemenid_small.xml:9
msgid ""
"\n"
"        Bolts of cloth, rugs and other high-quality textiles. Such crafts can be sold in bazars, and across the ancient world.\n"
"    "
msgstr ""
"\n"
"        Tygrullar, mattor och andra högkvalitativa textilier. Sådant hantverk kan säljas på basarer och i hela den antika världen.\n"
"    "

#: simulation/templates/gaia/treasure/metal_achaemenid_small.xml:8
msgid "Persian Rugs"
msgstr "Persiska mattor"

#: simulation/templates/gaia/treasure/metal_weapons_small.xml:8
msgid "Iron Weapons"
msgstr "Järnvapen"

#: simulation/templates/gaia/treasure/metal_weapons_small.xml:9
msgid ""
"\n"
"        A stash of weapons. Even if your soldiers have plenty of arms, the metal is good and could be used for other purposes.\n"
"    "
msgstr ""
"\n"
"        Ett vapenförråd. Även om dina soldater har gott om vapen är metallen användbar för andra ändamål.\n"
"    "

#: simulation/templates/gaia/treasure/pegasus.xml:8
msgid "Pegasus"
msgstr "Pegasus"

#: simulation/templates/gaia/treasure/pegasus.xml:9
msgid ""
"\n"
"        Legends say that Pegasus sprung from the decapitated body of Medusa and was the mount for the Hero Bellerophon when the hero fought the Chimera. Afterwards Bellerophon became haughty and tried to fly Pegasus to Mount Olympus. Zeus, the king of the Greek gods, sent a fly to drive Pegasus wild. Bellerophon was thrown off and lived the rest of his life blind, lame, and in poverty. Nothing more was said about Pegasus, at least until now. The famous horse would fetch a fine price if sold.\n"
"    "
msgstr ""
"\n"
"        Legenden säger att Pegasus sprang fram ur Medusas halshuggna kropp och bars av hjälten Bellerofon när han stred mot Chimaira. Därefter blev Bellerofon högmodig och försökte flyga Pegasus till Olympen. Zeus sände en fluga som skrämde Pegasus, Bellerofon kastades av och levde resten av sitt liv blind, halt och fattig. Inget mer sades om Pegasus, åtminstone inte förrän nu. Den berömda hästen skulle inbringa ett fint pris om den såldes.\n"
"    "

#: simulation/templates/gaia/treasure/shipwreck.xml:8
#: simulation/templates/gaia/treasure/shipwreck_ram_bow.xml:8
#: simulation/templates/gaia/treasure/shipwreck_sail_boat.xml:8
#: simulation/templates/gaia/treasure/shipwreck_sail_boat_cut.xml:8
msgid "Shipwreck"
msgstr "Skeppsvrak"

#: simulation/templates/gaia/treasure/shipwreck.xml:9
msgid ""
"\n"
"       Sadly, sailing in the ancient world could be a dangerous thing. Large storms could appear unexpectedly and wreck even the largest boat. It appears all the ship’s cargo has washed away. However, the ship’s wood is sturdy and could be repurposed.\n"
"    "
msgstr ""
"\n"
"       Sjöfart i den antika världen kunde vara farlig. Stora stormar kunde uppstå oväntat och förstöra även de största skeppen. Skeppets last har spolats bort, men virket är fortfarande starkt och kan återanvändas.\n"
"    "

#: simulation/templates/gaia/treasure/shipwreck_debris.xml:8
msgid "Shipwreck Cargo"
msgstr "Skeppsvrakslast"

#: simulation/templates/gaia/treasure/shipwreck_debris.xml:9
msgid ""
"\n"
"        Sadly, sailing in the ancient world was a dangerous thing. Large storms could appear unexpectedly and wreck even the largest boat. This is the cargo of some unfortunate boat. The boat isn't in sight. However, the saltwater hasn't gotten into the barrels and their contents are still edible.\n"
"    "
msgstr ""
"\n"
"        Sjöfart i den antika världen var farlig. Stora stormar kunde uppstå oväntat och förstöra även de största skeppen. Detta är lasten från ett olyckligt skepp. Skeppet syns inte till, men saltvattnet har inte trängt in i tunnorna och innehållet är fortfarande ätbart.\n"
"    "

#: simulation/templates/gaia/treasure/shipwreck_ram_bow.xml:9
msgid ""
"\n"
"       Sadly, sailing in the ancient world was a dangerous thing. Large storms could appear unexpectedly and wreck even the largest boat. It appears all the ship’s cargo has washed away. However, the ship’s wood is still sturdy and could be repurposed.\n"
"    "
msgstr ""
"\n"
"       Sjöfart i den antika världen var farlig. Stora stormar kunde uppstå oväntat och förstöra även de största skeppen. Skeppets last har spolats bort, men virket är fortfarande hållbart och kan återanvändas.\n"
"    "

#: simulation/templates/gaia/treasure/shipwreck_sail_boat.xml:9
#: simulation/templates/gaia/treasure/shipwreck_sail_boat_cut.xml:9
msgid ""
"\n"
"        Sadly, sailing in the ancient world was a dangerous thing. Storms came unexpectedly, and even the experienced fishermen could be driven onto the rocks. None of this ship’s supplies are salvageable, but the ship’s wood is still sound and could be repurposed.\n"
"    "
msgstr ""
"\n"
"        Sjöfart i den antika världen var farlig. Stormar kom oväntat och även erfarna fiskare kunde drivas upp på klipporna. Inga av skeppets förnödenheter går att bärga, men virket är fortfarande sunt och kan återanvändas.\n"
"    "

#: simulation/templates/gaia/treasure/special_argo.xml:8
msgid "The Argo"
msgstr "Argo"

#: simulation/templates/gaia/treasure/special_argo.xml:9
msgid "Mythological Treasure"
msgstr "Mytologisk skatt"

#: simulation/templates/gaia/treasure/special_argo.xml:10
msgid ""
"\n"
"        The Argo was the great ship of Jason and the Argonauts on their quest to find the golden fleece. Built by the command of Hera, the boat's figurehead was said to be an oracle. After the voyage, the boat was said to have collapsed on a disgraced Jason, killing him.\n"
"    "
msgstr ""
"\n"
"        Argo var Jasons och argonauternas stora skepp i deras sökande efter det gyllene skinnet. Skeppet byggdes på Heras befallning och dess galjonsfigur sades vara ett orakel. Efter färden sades skeppet ha rasat samman över den vanärade Jason och dödat honom.\n"
"    "

#: simulation/templates/gaia/treasure/special_argo.xml:13
msgid "The mythological ship of the hero Jason and his Argonauts."
msgstr "Hjälten Jasons och hans argonauters mytologiska skepp."

#: simulation/templates/gaia/treasure/standing_stone.xml:9
msgid ""
"\n"
"        A stone inscribed with mysterious symbols. They were placed for unknown reasons by ancient Britons.\n"
"    "
msgstr ""
"\n"
"        En sten med mystiska symboler. De placerades av okända skäl av forntida britanner.\n"
"    "

#: simulation/templates/gaia/treasure/stone.xml:8
msgid "Stone Treasure"
msgstr "Stenskatt"

#: simulation/templates/gaia/treasure/stone.xml:9
msgid ""
"\n"
"        This is a pile of stone roughly cut into blocks.\n"
"    "
msgstr ""
"\n"
"        Detta är en hög med sten som grovt huggits till block.\n"
"    "

#: simulation/templates/gaia/treasure/stone_pile_granite.xml:4
msgid "Cut Granite"
msgstr "Huggen granit"

#: simulation/templates/gaia/treasure/stone_pile_granite.xml:5
msgid ""
"\n"
"        A pile of granite roughly cut into blocks.\n"
"    "
msgstr ""
"\n"
"        En hög med granit som grovt huggits till block.\n"
"    "

#: simulation/templates/gaia/treasure/stone_pile_granite_large.xml:8
msgid "Cut Stone"
msgstr "Huggen sten"

#: simulation/templates/gaia/treasure/stone_pile_granite_large.xml:9
msgid ""
"\n"
"        A large pile of stone roughly cut into blocks.\n"
"    "
msgstr ""
"\n"
"        En stor hög med sten som grovt huggits till block.\n"
"    "

#: simulation/templates/gaia/treasure/stone_pile_red.xml:8
#: simulation/templates/gaia/treasure/stone_pile_sandstone.xml:4
msgid "Cut Sandstone"
msgstr "Huggen sandsten"

#: simulation/templates/gaia/treasure/stone_pile_red.xml:10
msgid ""
"\n"
"        A pile of red sandstone roughly cut into blocks.\n"
"    "
msgstr ""
"\n"
"        En hög med röd sandsten som grovt huggits till block.\n"
"    "

#: simulation/templates/gaia/treasure/stone_pile_sandstone.xml:6
msgid ""
"\n"
"        A pile of sandstone roughly cut into blocks.\n"
"    "
msgstr ""
"\n"
"        En hög med sandsten som grovt huggits till block.\n"
"    "

#: simulation/templates/gaia/treasure/wood.xml:8
msgid "Wood Treasure"
msgstr "Virkesskatt"

#: simulation/templates/gaia/treasure/wood.xml:9
msgid ""
"\n"
"        A pile of roughly hewn lumber.\n"
"    "
msgstr ""
"\n"
"        En hög med grovt hugget timmer.\n"
"    "

#: simulation/templates/gaia/treasure/wood_lumber.xml:8
msgid "Milled Lumber"
msgstr "Fräst timmer"

#: simulation/templates/gaia/treasure/wood_lumber.xml:9
msgid ""
"\n"
"        A pile of roughly hewn lumber, ready to be used.\n"
"    "
msgstr ""
"\n"
"        En hög med grovt hugget timmer, redo att användas.\n"
"    "

